# Attitude and yaw from the 62 s hover (log 00000035, 2026-11-03), tools/tuning/axis_id.py and
# tools/tuning/attitude_design.py. Long-data identification: roll K 81, pitch K 73 rad/s^2 per unit
# output, delay 52-55 ms (motors/props; the 0.7 s fit had 130 / 38 ms); yaw K ~8.5 (weak fit).
# Measured disturbance torque mostly 0.1-1 Hz (0.5 rad/s^2) and 1-3 Hz (0.4 rad/s^2).
# Model matched the flight (predicted 0.40/0.53 deg, flown 0.44 deg; heading 1.5 vs 1.9 deg).
# Roll/pitch: angle loop PM was 25-32 deg (x2.3-3.0 peak) = the visible 2.3 Hz rocking. Now rate PM
# 51-53, GM 6.6-7.0 dB, angle PM 52-57, angle error 0.42 deg worst axis; held at K x1.3, delay x1.15.
# Yaw: the angle loop (P 4.5) was faster than the yaw rate loop (crossover 1.5 rad/s): PM 12 deg,
# x5.3 peak = the visible rotation. Now heading 0.27 deg RMS predicted; stable for yaw K x0.5-2.0
# (rate PM >= 44, GM >= 6.5 dB).
# Before: ATC_RAT_RLL/PIT_P 0.15 _I 0.45 _D 0.002 _FLTD 15, ATC_ANG_RLL/PIT_P 9,
#         ATC_RAT_YAW_P 0.18 _I 0.018 _FLTE 2, ATC_ANG_YAW_P 4.5
